#: guide/en/wikitolearn-guide-chapter-10.txt:1
msgid ""
"WikiToLearn is actively developed both on the technical and the content side."
"\n"
"It's possible to contribute in several ways, regardless of the user's skills "
"and experience."
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/wikitolearn-guide-chapter-10.txt:1
msgid "Web development"
msgstr "Desendolcu web"

#: guide/en/wikitolearn-guide-chapter-10.txt:5
msgid ""
"There are lots of web app and applications developed by WikiToLearn.\n"
"Web development is split into groups and every group has its maintainer.\n"
"Take a look at http://meta.wikitolearn.org/Tech_Team and feel free to "
"contact the members to ask them more questions."
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/wikitolearn-guide-chapter-10.txt:5
msgid "Translation"
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/wikitolearn-guide-chapter-10.txt:10
msgid ""
"If you want to help with translation you can join the "
"[https://chat.wikitolearn.org/channel/translation #translation] channel."
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/wikitolearn-guide-chapter-10.txt:10
msgid "Bug tracking"
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/wikitolearn-guide-chapter-10.txt:13
msgid ""
"We use phabricator to keep tracks of our development and our bugs.\n"
"If you think you have found a bug and want to tell us about it, you need to "
"[https://identity.kde.org/index.php?r=registration/index register to KDE "
"identity] , log in into phabricator and "
"[https://phabricator.kde.org/maniphest/task/edit/form/1/?tags=WikiToLearn "
"create a ticket]."
msgstr ""

